      "text": "SITUATION NOW\nKyrgyzstan is preparing to launch its first homegrown satellite, which will be used to monitor agriculture. [1][4]\nKyrgyzstan's customs revenue has reached $1.8B. [3]\n\nWHAT THIS MEANS FOR KYRGYZSTAN\nThe domestic satellite for agriculture may improve crop monitoring and food security, but Kyrgyzstan is linked to 25 US OFAC and Canada SEMA sanctions designations. [4][E2]\n\nKEY RISKS\nKyrgyzstan's 25 US OFAC and Canada SEMA sanctions designations could deter foreign investment in its planned feed mills and storage facilities. [E2]\n\nWATCH ITEMS\nThe outcome of Kyrgyzstan's discussions with the EBRD on joint infrastructure projects in Bishkek remains unresolved. [5]",
